ompt": "Obtain memories for similar implementations using the research-bot:\n`research-bot(goals=\"<described implementation plan>\", desired_info=\"information on <files to be edited>. Memories relevant to what I am about to do. Focus on implementation and testing.\")`\n\nCritically examine implementation plan against memory findings:\n- Question assumptions about planned approach\n- Identify potential issues from similar past implementations\n- Consider if plan should be modified based on memory patterns\n- Challenge implementation assumptions and look for logical gaps\n- Determine if current approach is optimal given learned patterns\n- Look for contradictions between the plan and memories\n\nThink deeply about this before moving on.\n\nYou may use research bot multiple times if needed to gather more comprehensive information.\n\nDetermine if:\n- Research reveals new, contradictory, or missing information\n- Any part of the plan is not clear\n- More context is needed to implement the plan\n- You are not 100% sure the plan will be successful\n\nYou will present any new or clarified information to the user.\n", "safety_mode": "conversation_read_only", "navigation_choices": [{"go": "NEXT", "if": "research successful"}, {"else": "ASK_HELP"}]}, {"id": "Request Implementation Approval", "type": "wait_for_input", "prompt": "WHILE you have concerns identified in the previous step, discuss them with the user.\nELSE, present your understanding of the plan and the what was learned by research and ask:\n\"Is this understanding correct? Should I proceed with the implementation?\"\nWAIT FOR USER RESPONSE\n", "safety_mode": "conversation_read_only", "classify_response": {"no": ["no", "stop", "not yet"], "yes": ["yes", "proceed", "go ahead", "continue"], "else": ["*"], "unclear": ["kinda", "sorta", "I think", "probably"], "conditional": ["if", "but", "unless", "when", "maybe"]}, "navigation_choices": [{"go": "REPEAT_WITH_CLARIFICATION", "if": "conditional"}, {"go": "REPEAT_WITH_CLARIFICATION", "if": "unclear"}, {"go": "REPEAT_WITH_CLARIFICATION", "if": "no"}, {"go": "NEXT", "if": "yes"}, {"else": "REPEAT_WITH_CLARIFICATION"}]}, {"id": "Save Implementation Research", "type": "action", "prompt": "Save the research to a file in the issue folder:\n`~/github-issues/<owner>/<repo>/<issue-number>/implementation-research.md`\n\nThis file should be a dump of what was returned by the research bot, but:\n- Remove any information that is an exact duplicate of the project plan information\n- Remove any incorrect or misleading information that have come from memories\n- Add on any new or clarified information that was provided by the user\n", "safety_mode": "unrestricted", "navigation_choices": [{"go": "NEXT", "if": "file saved successfully"}, {"else": "ASK_HELP"}]}, {"id": "Implement First Task", "type": "action", "prompt": "This step is the start of a loop. It is critical that you only implement one task at a time and then move to the next step in the process. NEVER implement multiple tasks in this step.\n\nEvery time you enter this step, you will:\n\n1. Get the next unfinished task from the project plan (if any)\n  - A task is not finished until it is verified by the am-i-done bot\n  - All validations specified in the project plan must be in the PASSED or SKIPPED state to be considered complete\n  - NEVER move to the next task until all prior tasks are complete\n2. Do the Work for this task, but NOT the Validation (am-i-done bot will do that in the next step)\n\nOptionally, you may use the `mcp__internal__coder-bot` to perform work if desired, but be sure that you:\n  - Only use it for simple work\n  - Always commit changes before calling the bot, this will allow you to see the changes made and revert if needed\n  - Provide clear instructions with appropriate context\n  - You MUST repeat all critical instructions on each call, it will not remember previous instructions\n  - Be sure to provide the path to the project plan and tell it which task you are working on\n  - Provide the path to the implementation research file you created in the previous step\n  - Review the bot's response\n  - If the bot did not complete the task but offered no explanation why, it might have run out of context space\n    - Call it again with the same instructions, but inform it that this is the second pass and the Task is partially complete\n    - Alter the files list you provide to reflect which files are remaining to be changed\n    - For any files you are unsure about, list them as \"update\" and note that the completion status is unknown\n  - If the bot seemed to fail, undo the changes it made and call it again with better instructions\n\nALWAYS COMMIT CHANGES BEFORE MOVING ON TO THE NEXT STEP\n", "safety_mode": "unrestricted", "navigation_choices": [{"go": "NEXT", "if": "task completed according to plan"}, {"else": "ASK_HELP"}]}, {"id": "Run Validation", "type": "action", "prompt": "Call the am-i-done bot to validate implementation:\n\nFor first validation call:\n```\nmcp__internal__am-i-done-bot({\n  new_conversation: {\n    goal: \"<path/to/project-plan.md><all goals not in project plan>\",\n    context: \"<files changed, work summary, detailed context including previous validation learnings>\"\n  }\n})\n```\n\nFor clarification follow-up calls:\n```\nmcp__internal__am-i-done-bot({\n  continue_conversation: {\n    message: \"<answers to bot's questions based on available context>\"\n  }\n})\n```\n", "safety_mode": "prescribed_execution", "navigation_choices": [{"go": "REPEAT_WITH_CLARIFICATION", "if": "NEEDS CLARIFICATION and answers are known from context"}, {"go": "Get Clarification from User", "if": "NEEDS CLARIFICATION and answers are unknown"}, {"go": "Fix Issues", "if": "FINAL REPORT and any validation category is FAILED, BLOCKED, or MISSING"}, {"go": "Implement Next Task", "if": "FINAL REPORT, ALL validation categories are PASSED or SKIPPED, more tasks remain"}, {"go": "Coderabbit Review", "if": "FINAL REPORT, ALL valida