LP"}]}, {"id": "Critical Assessment", "type": "action", "prompt": "# 1. Talk to the Thought-Partner Bot\n\nHave a conversation with the thought-partner bot to deepen your reasoning and conclusions. This is the most important step in the analysis process. You must always give this your deepest attention and ultra-think. You should expect a multi turn conversation, do not stop until you have thought through all points and reach agreement with your thought-partner.\n\nRemember that the thought-partner bot is a tool and not the user. It has no authority to make decisions for you. It is just a second opinion from a trusted advisor. Do not let it steer you away from the user provided restraints and goals.\n\n## First Iteration\nThe very first time you call the thought-partner bot, you should provide something like this example:\n```\nmcp__internal__thought-partner-bot({\n  \"new_conversation\": {\n    \"goals\": \"I need you to critically examine my analysis of <short-descriptive-name>. I've recorded my research and analysis in <absolute path to folder>. Please read these files and help me identify gaps, biases, or flawed reasoning.\",\n    \"desired_info\": \"After reading my analysis at <path-to-folder>/01/analysis.md, I need to know: 1) Are my root cause analyses accurate or am I missing deeper architectural issues? 2) Will my proposed solutions actually fix the problems or just create new failure modes? 3) Am I treating symptoms vs root causes? 4) What unintended consequences might my recommendations create? 5) Are there simpler solutions I'm overlooking? The research data is also available at /home/user/claude-instructions/analysis/2025-01-17-am-i-done-bot-issues/01/research.txt if you need it.\",\n    \"session_name\": \"<short-descriptive-name>-critical-assessment\",\n    \"max_tool_uses\": 10\n  }\n})\n```\n\nOn subsequent calls, you should continue the conversation the `continue_conversation` field.\n\n## Subsequent Iterations\nWhen you loop back on a new iterati